    <mxCell id="t2_inland" value="&lt;b&gt;✓ OPTIMIZED — Detailed Options from G_fine (actual schedules + spot rates):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;[A] Direct Truck (OHL) — depart Jul 4 16:00, arrive Jul 5 09:00 — $612 ✓ SELECTED&lt;br&gt;[B] Drayage to Compton + Rail — depart Jul 4 20:00, arrive Jul 6 08:00 — $389&lt;br&gt;[C] Expedite (FedEx Custom Critical) — depart Jul 4 14:30, arrive Jul 4 22:00 — $1,480" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="325" y="365" width="535" height="85" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>

    <!-- ===== KEY INSIGHT ===== -->
    <mxCell id="insight" value="&lt;b&gt;Key Design Principle:&lt;/b&gt; The system maintains a complete end-to-end plan at all times. Future legs are cost/time envelopes on a coarse graph G_coarse — sufficient for the objective function but not execution. As the shipment advances and uncertainty decreases, each leg is re-solved on G_fine with actual carrier schedules, port clearance estimates, and live spot rates. The re-plan trigger fires when confidence in the upstream leg&apos;s arrival time exceeds a threshold. This is Model Predictive Control applied to multimodal freight routing." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="50" y="465" width="810" height="80" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>

